# Sparring Dummy ({1}{G}, 1/3 defender): "{T}: Mill a card. You may put a land card milled this way into your hand." It cannot attack
# (defender; the Ornithopter, which can, is asked about and attacks). In turn 3 the card milled is an Island: Bot1 may take it (the first answer is refused, no Memnite is offered), it goes to
# the hand, and the Dummy is tapped so a second activation is refused. In turn 5 the card milled is an Ornithopter: nothing is asked
# (! Choose), it stays in the graveyard, and no life is gained (it is no Lesson card). Only one card is milled each time.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Emerald
Mox Ruby
Sparring Dummy
Ornithopter x4
Memnite
Island
Memnite
Ornithopter
Forest x9

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Sparring Dummy.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T3 Bot1.DeclareAttackers]
! Bot1.Attack(Sparring Dummy > Bot2)
Bot1.Attack(Ornithopter > Bot2)
[T3 Bot1.Main2]
Bot1.Battlefield.Sparring Dummy.Activate
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
! Bot1.Choose(Memnite)
Bot1.Choose(Island)
? Bot1.Graveyard.Count = 0
? Bot1.Hand = Island; Memnite; Ornithopter; Ornithopter; Ornithopter
! Bot1.Battlefield.Sparring Dummy.Activate
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Sparring Dummy.Activate
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
! Bot1.Choose

[Expect]
Bot1.Graveyard = Ornithopter
Bot1.Life = 20
Bot1.Library.Count = 9
